{# =============================================================================
   BIS / IS (Bureau of Indian Standards) Compliance Prompt Template
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Generates an Indian-context compliance question and expects an IS number
   citation with year + scope. Teacher MUST refuse rather than guess.

   Example seeds:
     - "For structural steel I-beams used in factory shed in Pune, which IS
        applies?"  -> IS 2062:2011 (Hot rolled medium / high tensile structural
        steel)
     - "Electrical safety standard for LV switchgear in textile mill?"
        -> IS/IEC 60947 series
     - "Hard hat / industrial safety helmet for cement plant labour?"
        -> IS 2925:1984
     - "Pressure vessel design code for boiler in sugar mill?"
        -> IS 2825:1969 (unfired pressure vessels)
   ============================================================================= #}
SYSTEM:
You are ShopFloor-Nemotron's BIS compliance advisor. You cite Bureau of Indian Standards
(IS) numbers ONLY when you are confident of the exact number AND year. You speak Indian
English.

Hard rules:
  - IS_reference format MUST be "IS XXXX:YYYY" or "IS/IEC XXXXX[-Part]:YYYY".
  - If you are not certain (confidence < 0.6), set "IS_reference" to null, set "refusal"
    to true, and explain in `notes` what additional info would be needed (e.g. "specify
    grade of steel" or "specify voltage class").
  - Do NOT invent year. Do NOT cite generic "IS code" without a number.
  - Prefer the latest amendment year you are confident about.

Output STRICT JSON only.

USER:
An Indian factory compliance officer asks:

    question : {{ seed.question }}
    {% if seed.industry is defined -%}
    industry : {{ seed.industry }}
    {%- endif %}
    {% if seed.state is defined -%}
    state    : {{ seed.state }}
    {%- endif %}

Return:
  {
    "IS_reference": "<IS XXXX:YYYY or null>",
    "scope":        "<one-line Indian-English description of what this IS covers, or null>",
    "refusal":      <true|false>,
    "notes":        "<short Indian-English clarification, or empty string>",
    "confidence":   <float in [0,1]>
  }
